    "evidenceByGoal": "Ulcerative colitis: Design: open-label trial. Population: patients with moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis (Mayo score ≥6 and endoscopic subscore ≥1). Sample size: 13 participants completed the study and 11 were evaluable for clinical response. Dose and duration: oral TUDCA 1.75 or 2 g/day for 6 weeks. Comparator: not verified in reviewed source. Outcomes: the source reports significant improvement in clinical, endoscopic, and histologic disease activity at week 6, with mean total Mayo Score changing from 9 to 4.5 (p<0.001), alongside reduced ER stress and inflammation and increased markers of epithelial restitution. [38] Adverse events: TUDCA was well-tolerated, with transient dyspepsia reported as the most common side effect. [38] Key limitation: small, open-label study; only 13 participants completed and 11 were evaluable. [38]\n\nAmyotrophic lateral sclerosis: Design: proof-of-principle study providing preliminary data. Population: patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. Sample size, dose, duration, comparator, and specific adverse events: not verified in reviewed source. Outcome: preliminary efficacy and tolerability data were sought in a series of patients. [38] Key limitation: the reviewed summary characterizes the evidence as preliminary and based on a patient series. [38]",
