    "evidenceByGoal": "Dyslipidemia/lipid profile: (1) Amlamax™ (a purified, standardized dried amla extract containing about 35% galloellagi tannins) was assessed in a pilot clinical study of human volunteers; 500 mg/day and 1000 mg/day were evaluated for 6 months. The supplied record reports reduced total and LDL cholesterol, increased HDL cholesterol, and reduced CRP. Sample size, comparator, adverse events, and key limitation were not verified in the reviewed source. [43] (2) Amla capsule was compared with simvastatin in 60 type II hyperlipidemic patients: 40 received Amla 500 mg daily and 20 received simvastatin 20 mg daily for 42 days. The record reports reductions in total cholesterol, LDL, triglycerides, and VLDL, with increased HDL in both groups. Comparator details beyond the stated simvastatin group, adverse events, and key limitation were not verified in the reviewed source. [44]\n\nInflammatory marker: In the Amlamax™ pilot study, blood CRP was reported to be significantly reduced after the intervention. Sample size, comparator, adverse events, and key limitation were not verified in the reviewed source. [43]\n\nBlood pressure: In the Amla-versus-simvastatin study, both treatments were reported to significantly reduce blood pressure, with the effect described as more marked in the Amla group. Adverse events and key limitation were not verified in the reviewed source. [44]",
